TI  - Data-Aided Channel Estimation for Robust DECT-2020 NR+ Links in Oil and Gas Equipment Data Communication
AU  - Liu, Zheyuan
AU  - Li, Qian
AU  - Yang, Shuangye
AU  - Yao, Chenyang
AU  - Zhao, Kai
AU  - Jia, Lufeng
AU  - Zhang, Qiao
AU  - Guo, Biao
T2  - 2025 7th International Conference on Intelligent Control, Measurement and Signal Processing (ICMSP)
AB  - Oil and gas extraction and processing environments impose stringent requirements on wireless data links used for equipment monitoring, control, and safety. Multipath-rich metallic structures, Radio Frequency(RF) blocking, and dynamic interference degrade channel estimation accuracy, especially at low SNR. This paper adapts and evaluates a data-aided least-squares (LS) channel estimation approach—originally developed and validated for Digital Enhancement Cordless Telecommunication2020 New Radio Plus(DECT-2020 NR+)—to oil and gas equipment data communication over Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing(OFDM) links. By combining pilot symbols with previously decoded data symbols, the proposed receiver improves channel transfer function (CTF) estimates without increasing pilot overhead. MATLAB simulations on AWGN and 3GPP TDL channels, coupled with a lab validation using a DECT development board and a backscatter-like test signal, show consistent MSE gains over pilot-only LS across SNRs. Deployment aspects for oil and gas sites, including subcarrier numerology, packetization, and frequency planning in the 1.9 GHz frequency band, which is used in some industrial wireless systems. Detailed implementation guidance is provided for field gateways and sensor Radio Devices(RDs). Results indicate that data-aided estimation enhances reliability and spectral efficiency for real-time equipment telemetry and alarm reporting in harsh oilfield environments.
