TI  - A Pareto Optimality Approach for Link Adaptation in DECT NR+
AU  - Graf, Fabian
AU  - Villnow, Michael
AU  - Watteyne, Thomas
T2  - 2026 IEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference (WCNC)
AB  - DECT NR+ is a novel wireless IoT standard operating in the 1.9 GHz band, a band originally reserved for Digital Enhanced Cordless Telecommunications (DECT). This technology is also announced as the first non-cellular 5 G standard and theoretically offers wide flexibility in its application, ranging from Wireless Personal Area Network (WPAN) to Wide Area Network (WAN) scenarios. While this versatility is enabled by a wide range of configurable parameters, the practical application range is determined by the vendor's specific implementation. In this article, we investigate the impact of adjusting Modulation and Coding Scheme (MCS), transmit power and packet length. We formulate objective functions for data rate, energy consumption, and Packet Delivery Ratio (PDR), and analyze their dependence on the aforementioned parameters. To model specific relationships, we conduct practical experiments in two real-world testbeds using hardware from the Nordic nRF91 series. Finally, we present an approach for parameter selection based on the principle of Pareto optimality.
